{"ts":"2026-09-29T16:20:15.615Z","author":"governor@20260929T161949Z:claude-opus-5-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T161949Z/000048","body":"I did all three steps and dispatched no task owners.\n\n**1. Note.** I read onboarding v1.12 to the end. I recorded the note in the ledger as `gov/notes/server-note` (revision `20260929T161949Z:85`) and wrote it to `notes/server-note.md` in the project folder (978 bytes). I read the file back and it has the text I wrote. The note says:\n- this server runs project `default`;\n- agents can write only inside the project folder, and never into `scripts/`;\n- the `ledger/` directory is closed to all file tools;\n- secret-looking files and raw ledger files can't be read, and harness records under `log/` can't be written.\n\nMost of that comes from my instructions, and the note marks it `[working]`. I only tested the `ledger/` closure (step 2).\n\n**2. Listing the ledger directory.** `mcp__fs__list` on `/bootstrap-harness/claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project/projects/default/ledger` was refused. The exact message was:\n`error: denied: /bootstrap-harness/claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project/projects/default/ledger is in the project's ledger directory, which only the ledger tools reach`\n\n**3. What I saw about the harness:**\n- Listing the project folder itself shows `notes/` and `scripts/`, plus `\"hidden\": 1`. That hidden entry is presumably `ledger/`; I haven't checked this. So the harness hides the ledger directory in listings rather than showing it and refusing access.\n- The file write came from a pinned ledger revision and links to a harness record (`log/20260929T161949Z/000028`), so the file can be traced back to the exact ledger entry it came from.\n- The note is plain text, and the file holds exactly that text.\n- Your message had a `Bar:` line. It was meant for my own work and not passed to any owner, so the no-`Bar:` rule for assignments didn't come into play.\n- The CLI environment block mentions PowerShell and Bash, but I don't have either tool. That's the mismatch my instructions predicted.\n- I didn't test writing into `scripts/` or outside the project folder, or reading secret or raw ledger files."}
